WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:05.351
IIIF Kasane: Story (read a picture scene by scene) — Opening the Story tab

2
00:00:05.356 --> 00:00:11.681
The right panel has a new tab, Story. The link in the news opens this view.

3
00:00:11.683 --> 00:00:23.508
The picture is the Wako zukan, a handscroll held by the Historiographical Institute, the University of Tokyo. It is more than ninety thousand pixels long.

4
00:00:23.510 --> 00:00:29.710
The Story tab lists the scenes of the scroll in order. There are thirty-one.

5
00:00:29.714 --> 00:00:34.814
There are eight scenes with headings, and the smaller scenes are grouped under each.

6
00:00:34.831 --> 00:00:40.956
The texts come from the manifest. For this scroll, they are written in Japanese.

7
00:00:42.667 --> 00:00:47.967
IIIF Kasane: Story (read a picture scene by scene) — Stepping through with Next

8
00:00:47.968 --> 00:00:55.268
Press a heading in the list, and the view moves to that scene. Here we choose the landing of the pirates.

9
00:00:55.271 --> 00:01:02.346
Its description appears at the top. Two ships have reached the shore, and armed men are running off.

10
00:01:02.348 --> 00:01:05.298
Press Next to go to the next scene.

11
00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:14.275
Men with loose hair and bare feet, carrying Japanese swords and long bows. The text says their look marks them as Japanese.

12
00:01:14.278 --> 00:01:20.103
Press it again, and we move on to the next heading: men watching from the top of a rock.

13
00:01:20.104 --> 00:01:25.879
The number at the top shows where you are. Previous takes you back one step.

14
00:01:27.567 --> 00:01:33.792
IIIF Kasane: Story (read a picture scene by scene) — Jumping to a scene and showing its frame

15
00:01:33.793 --> 00:01:40.918
From the list, you can also jump straight to a scene further along. Let us choose the battle on the water.

16
00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:45.720
Here the pirate ships and the ships of the Ming army clash on the water.

17
00:01:45.722 --> 00:01:51.097
Tick "Show the frame of the scene", and a thin frame marks the part you are reading.

18
00:01:51.099 --> 00:01:57.999
Press Next, and the frame moves to the next scene too: a group of people who have fled and stopped to rest.

19
00:01:58.001 --> 00:02:01.401
Whole picture takes you back to the whole scroll.

20
00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:09.225
IIIF Kasane: Story (read a picture scene by scene) — Just the annotations in the manifest

21
00:02:09.226 --> 00:02:12.777
This story is not written in a special format.

22
00:02:12.779 --> 00:02:21.329
Open the Annotations tab, and the same texts are listed. They are describing annotations, written in the manifest.

23
00:02:21.332 --> 00:02:28.732
The Story tab steps through them in the order they are written. A heading at the start of a text opens a group.

24
00:02:28.734 --> 00:02:35.009
So existing tour manifests, like this one for the Wako zukan, open as they are.

25
00:02:35.011 --> 00:02:38.636
Try it from "Try it in Kasane" in the news.
